etting words I say  geez you know am I getting older now am  I am I not able to learn this language  and then I say well no  just think back five months ago when I  started I thought that I will never  learn to read the Arabic writing system  because there were four different forms  of each each symbol each letter and  there's no you know consonants or like  hardly any and stuff so yeah I look back  to where I was and Here I am five months  later actually I'm doing quite well and  I mean I'm reading some fairly difficult  stuff granted with the help of of you  know link and stuff like that I'm  plowing my way through SML I've gone  through all 76 lessons once for forget  all the words I'm going back through now  around 45 46 going through it again I am  getting somewhere  so yes I am confident that I can learn  Arabic whether my brain cells have  slowed down or my cognitive ability is  not what it was when I was 20 is kind of  irrelevant it's like this discussion  about whether some people are better  than others at learning or whether kids  are better or older people are better it  really doesn't matter as long as you can  learn you know some people will learn  faster and some people slower and some  people will be better at some aspects of  the language and others will be better  at other aspects so it doesn't matter so  yeah I am confident that I will learn  Arabic however long it takes me and I'm  enjoying it so that but that confidence  that you can get there is extremely  important it's also important to be  confident that it's worthwhile that that  you are doing something that is  important that matters that is gonna be  beneficial to you in some personal way  because you don't want to be doing  something and then second-guessing jeez  is it really you know for example when I  tell people that I'm learning Arabic  they look at me as if I'm a lunatic you  know a like why would you why would you  take that on and be you speak all these  other languages is now you're gonna have  to neglect these languages to learn  Arabic why are you doing it but then  again you know as I you know listen to  or read these stories in Arabic Arab  people speaking to each other  about things that are related to their  culture or part of their daily life and  I'm able to understand it and the other  day there was a tweet by someone that I  follow on Twitter and it had a headline  from an Egyptian newspaper and I was  able to read it alone I missed the odd  word a--basically I was able to read it  and I get great satisfaction so yeah I'm  confident that it is worth my while to  be learning of course the other  confidence is are you confident that the  way you are learning the method you're  using is effective is this the best way  to learn here again that becomes very  subjective I enjoy the way I learn I  know that there are inefficiencies I  know for example that I tend to listen  to you know I've got these various  sources or resources that I'm using I've  got them on my iPhone so I will tend to  listen if I'm in the car for half an  hour for an hour a day I'll be listening  through lots of these stories and I miss  a lot of words if I were trying to be  efficient I would probably focus on one  story a little more listen to it don't  understand go right back and read it  again go back and listen again so that I  would get more concentration but  realistically that's not how my day  develops the way my day develops is I go  somewhere in my car doesn't do half an  hour and then I come back I listen to  half an hour then I sit down and maybe  spend another 20 minutes half an hour on  my computer so these activities are  disjointed so I recognize that the way  I'm learning is perhaps not the most  efficient way but it's it's a way that  conforms to my other activities daily  activities it's a way that makes sense  for me it's not as efficient as it could  be but I'm confident that it's it's  essentially gonna get me to my  destination so I think it is important  that that we be confident that we can  learn the language that it's worth while  doing so and that the method we are  using is appropriate and if we have  those three  kinds of confidences you know then we  will learn we will acquire words we will  enjoy the language and at some point we  will speak and some will speak earlier  and some will speak later and some was  beat with more confidence than some will  speak with less confidence but that  confidence to speak to my mind in the  long run  ever think about learning the language  that confidence to speak is less  important than this confidence that you  can achieve your goal that you're doing  it the right way and that it's  worthwhile doing so there are some  thoughts on confidence so I am confident  that I can learn the learn Arabic I'm  and other languages that are going to  learn I'm not so confident that my  cognitive powers are you know not worse  than they were when I was 20 years old  but I don't care okay thank you for  listening bye for now  [Music]
 

